Then the finished panels are cut to size with a high pressure water jet.

440
00:37:38,140 --> 00:37:40,960
Much cooler, much easier than steel.

441
00:37:40,961 --> 00:37:47,960
The composite has been used to form the Visby into a stunningly original stealth shape,

442
00:37:47,961 --> 00:37:51,960
with angles that can bounce threatening radar signals away from the ship.

443
00:37:51,961 --> 00:37:54,960
The exterior of the ship is completely clean.

444
00:37:54,961 --> 00:37:58,960
Nothing is allowed topside to betray Visby to an enemy's radar.

445
00:37:59,960 --> 00:38:05,960
But Visby's designers are aware that the sensor of the future may not be radar.

446
00:38:05,961 --> 00:38:12,340
Visby is powered by water jet propulsion that offers less noise for acoustic weapons to home in on.

447
00:38:12,960 --> 00:38:17,920
And special attention has been paid to eliminating heat to avoid infrared detection.

448
00:38:19,420 --> 00:38:21,440
The Swede's success is amazing.

449
00:38:22,100 --> 00:38:25,580
Above is an infrared targeting image of a conventional ship.

450
00:38:26,040 --> 00:38:29,940
Below is the heat image of Visby, all but invisible.

451
00:38:29,941 --> 00:38:37,940
The whole idea with the stealth philosophy on Visby is to reduce the detection range

452
00:38:37,941 --> 00:38:46,200
significantly, in many cases 50% or 70%, that allows the commander to decide if he wants

453
00:38:46,201 --> 00:38:53,380
to shoot or hide or wait or go into some other mode of operation.

454
00:38:53,381 --> 00:38:58,560
Another Scandinavian country is also pushing the envelope of stealth design on a dramatic

455
00:38:58,561 --> 00:39:04,200
coastline cut by narrow fjords and dotted with hundreds of islands, a new class of stealth

456
00:39:04,201 --> 00:39:07,140
ship lies waiting to defend Norway.

457
00:39:11,880 --> 00:39:18,680
Her name is Scholl, Norwegian for shield, and this seagoing speedster is something special.

458
00:39:21,300 --> 00:39:25,960
Scholl is driven by water jets at an incredible speed of over 50 knots.

459
00:39:25,961 --> 00:39:31,460
Just like the Swede's Fisbee class, she is built of lightweight composite, and her hull

460
00:39:31,461 --> 00:39:37,460
and superstructure are also smooth and angled, offering a poor target for enemy radar.

461
00:39:37,461 --> 00:39:41,460
Joel rides over the water on an air-cushioned catamaran hull.

462
00:39:41,461 --> 00:39:46,960
This new ship compared to a conventional hull has a lot of advantages.

463
00:39:46,961 --> 00:39:48,960
It has much higher speed.

464
00:39:48,961 --> 00:39:51,960
It has better sea-keeping performances.

465
00:39:51,961 --> 00:39:56,960
This ship is hard to detect on a radar because it's built by stealth principles.

466
00:39:56,961 --> 00:40:02,960
But all of these innovative vessels offer only a hint of what stealthy warships may

467
00:40:02,961 --> 00:40:04,960
look like in the future.

468
00:40:04,961 --> 00:40:09,960
Work is already underway in the US Navy to create a whole new generation of stealthy

469
00:40:09,961 --> 00:40:10,960
vessels.

470
00:40:10,961 --> 00:40:18,960
Leading the way will be a revolutionary ship that today is known only as the DDX.

471
00:40:18,961 --> 00:40:22,960
DDX will look unlike any other ship ever built.

472
00:40:22,961 --> 00:40:25,960
A radically slanting hull will deflect radar.

473
00:40:25,961 --> 00:40:28,960
Her decks will be barren of anything that could give away her presence.

474
00:40:28,961 --> 00:40:31,960
No sailor will normally be allowed on deck.

475
00:40:31,961 --> 00:40:35,960
For most of her crew, life aboard will be like serving in a submarine.

476
00:40:35,961 --> 00:40:39,960
Missiles will be dispersed and hidden in the ship's sides.

477
00:40:39,961 --> 00:40:50,960
Her mass will be stealthily concealed inside a sleek superstructure.

478
00:40:50,961 --> 00:40:56,840
DDX will be propelled by electric motors that give off considerably less noise to betray

479
00:40:56,841 --> 00:40:59,240
the new ship's position.

480
00:40:59,241 --> 00:41:04,460
The first DDX is expected to join the US fleet in 2013.

481
00:41:04,461 --> 00:41:11,460
One of her missions will be to work close to shore to offer gunfire support to land forces.

482
00:41:11,461 --> 00:41:16,460
In future planning, Marines will be dropped behind enemy lines with lightning speed.

483
00:41:16,461 --> 00:41:23,460
To do this, they will carry less of their own artillery and rely more on the guns of DDX.

484
00:41:23,461 --> 00:41:27,460
Guns that are as stealthy as they are devastating.

485
00:41:27,461 --> 00:41:32,100
The barrel of the 155-millimeter gun is hidden until it rises.

486
00:41:32,620 --> 00:41:35,840
To blast 10 shells a minute over 100 miles,

487
00:41:36,160 --> 00:41:39,040
once fired, satellites will guide the shells to their target

488
00:41:39,041 --> 00:41:41,440
with an accuracy measured in yards.

489
00:41:42,920 --> 00:41:46,940
When finished firing, the barrel again hides from radar detection.

490
00:41:48,320 --> 00:41:53,760
DDX will be so highly automated that she will be crewed by as few as 125 sailors,

491
00:41:53,761 --> 00:41:57,520
less than half that required by today's ships of her size.

492
00:41:58,420 --> 00:42:04,560
The Navy is also developing a close relative of DDX, the Littoral Combat Ship, or LCS.

493
00:42:05,180 --> 00:42:08,740
Three companies are currently competing to design this radically new ship.

494
00:42:09,800 --> 00:42:13,760
If built, LCS will engage in anti-submarine patrols, mine countermeasures,

495
00:42:14,680 --> 00:42:18,480
and launching and recovering secret special ops teams, such as SEALs.

496
00:42:19,680 --> 00:42:23,040
LCS will sail into battle at speeds of up to 50 knots,

497
00:42:23,041 --> 00:42:25,940
and will be as stealthy as any ship in the world.

498
00:42:27,320 --> 00:42:32,900
Both DDX and the Latoro combat ship will lead us to a whole new world of stealthy warships.

499
00:42:33,760 --> 00:42:37,060
Amphibious landing ships, the ugly ducklings of the old Navy,

500
00:42:37,061 --> 00:42:40,480
will feature stealthy-shaped masts and smooth surfaces.

501
00:42:41,820 --> 00:42:45,960
SEAL teams will sneak ashore riding in a stealthy underwater delivery vehicle.

502
00:42:46,440 --> 00:42:49,880
When their mission is completed, it will carry them back to a mother submarine.

503
00:42:49,881 --> 00:42:56,120
It is safe to say that in the navy of the future, most ships will be dominated by stealth

504
00:42:56,121 --> 00:42:57,120
technology.

505
00:42:57,121 --> 00:43:02,120
Shapes will remind you some of a spacecraft perhaps is the best term, but if you look

506
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:06,480
at airplanes you get a good idea of where we're going with ships.

507
00:43:06,481 --> 00:43:12,260
And for the future I think you'll see that same sort of transition in the shape of ships.

508
00:43:12,261 --> 00:43:15,900
I'm not sure I can visualize the actual shape of a warship in a hundred years time, but I

509
00:43:15,901 --> 00:43:17,380
I can tell you some of the things it will be.

510
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:19,360
It will be submersible.

511
00:43:19,900 --> 00:43:22,740
I think that all warships will be capable of going under the surface.

512
00:43:23,260 --> 00:43:24,420
I think it will be fast.

513
00:43:24,940 --> 00:43:26,280
I think it will be cost-effective.

514
00:43:26,520 --> 00:43:28,320
In other words, it will have a propulsion system

515
00:43:28,321 --> 00:43:30,180
which will allow it to stay at sea longer.

516
00:43:30,620 --> 00:43:32,860
I think it will have fewer crew.

517
00:43:34,040 --> 00:43:35,940
Ships may become fully automated,

518
00:43:35,941 --> 00:43:40,200
sailing across oceans and carrying out their missions with no crew at all.

519
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:43,080
Use of lightweight composites and hull designs,

520
00:43:43,081 --> 00:43:46,540
such as catamarans, trimarans, and surface effects,

521
00:43:46,880 --> 00:43:50,140
will allow ships to hit speeds of almost 100 knots.

522
00:43:52,240 --> 00:43:57,400
Whatever their size or mission, warships will possess new levels of stealth capability

523
00:43:57,401 --> 00:44:00,100
that will make them increasingly hard to detect.

524
00:44:00,760 --> 00:44:06,120
But as research continues on stealth, so too does research on ways to beat it.

525
00:44:07,260 --> 00:44:11,080
So you've always got this balance of trying to get more stealthy,

526
00:44:11,081 --> 00:44:15,696
stealthy, trying to get better sensors or exploit another signature.

527
00:44:15,697 --> 00:44:17,800
And this has been the nature of

528
00:44:17,801 --> 00:44:22,190
warfare. Swords, they develop shields to protect themselves from it.

529
00:44:22,191 --> 00:44:23,740
And now it's you build a

530
00:44:23,741 --> 00:44:25,774
better missile or a more stealthy ship.

531
00:44:25,775 --> 00:44:28,800
The other side is going to look for countermeasures to it.

532
00:44:29,660 --> 00:44:35,640
The dangerous game of cat and mouse will continue as warships search for ways to elude enemy

533
00:44:35,641 --> 00:44:37,240
detection with invisibility.

534
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:39,600
And many of the answers will continue

535
00:44:39,601 --> 00:44:41,380
to be found in new technology

536
00:44:41,381 --> 00:44:43,460
offering a chance for the greatest

537
00:44:43,461 --> 00:44:45,720
of human weapons, the ship at sea

538
00:44:45,721 --> 00:44:47,640
to disappear behind

539
00:44:47,641 --> 00:44:49,700
the magic curtain of stealth.

